1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,160
So for those who don't know, I went to Cuba for the last week with the organization IFCO, Pastors for Peace.

2
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:20,560
I think for some people, they think solidarity is simply just like, you know, giving stuff to people who need it.

3
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:23,200
That is charity.

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:47,900
Solidarity is showing support beyond material goods, but also in values in order to protect the efforts that are being laid out on the ground and that have caused the need for the support.

5
00:00:47,900 --> 00:01:05,920
So when we look at Cuba and we understand that Cuba has suffered greatly for standing against imperialism, we remember that many of us are benefiting from imperialism in many a way.

6
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:25,640
And so the solidarity is shown because it is also us knowing that it is our responsibility as people who are benefiting, even if we are not the ones enacting it, to do the counter work that our government is doing.

7
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:31,900
We should be acting against the way that our government is committing harm.

8
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:37,960
If we want to say that we are not our government, it is just the United States.

9
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:42,740
If we want to be on that wave, then we have to actually do that in action.

10
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,840
We have to do that, not just with our voice.

11
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:47,480
We have to do that with our funds.

12
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:48,680
We have to do that with our time.

13
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,940
We have to do that with our bodies, et cetera, et cetera, et cetera.

14
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:59,300
Because I know for me, there's been a human to human concept around it.

15
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:24,780
But I had kind of missed the necessity to show up in solidarity because this nation has carried out a revolution that demonstrated for us that which we have yet to be seen in our own country, but that we should see in our own country.

16
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:28,700
Free health care, access to schooling, et cetera.

17
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,060
We've got to be a better way.

18
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:43,940
We've got to be a better way.

